embership is latest-versus-committed: new leader changes wait for a committed current-term entry and stable configuration, then update voter aggregation and all-peer replication; retained voter IDs preserve their slots. Followers roll back latest configuration on suffix conflict and recover configuration from snapshot/logs. Snapshot installation supplies a prefix match only after storage/FSM restore and response processing; application queueing is distinct from completed application. VerifyLeader uses a separate Boolean notification path and must not be equated with commitment. User Restore is an explicitly restricted disaster-recovery override with aborted inflight futures and a later no-op completion.', ['b-leader-life','b-config','b-vote','b-recover','b-install','b-user-restore','b-verify'],['f-match','f-vote-granted','f-verification-notification'],['s-leader-life','s-commitment','s-repl-ownership','s-config-change','s-rpc','s-vote','s-startup','s-install','s-restore-contract']),core_gaps=[],open_details=['Network heartbeat concurrent context-write interleavings versus main loop; source comments and wiring differ.','VerifyLeader suffrage filtering, response timing and applicable authority contract need discrimination.','Heartbeat contact versus higher-term reply handling: other workers and negative verification may protect authority.','Pipeline error/partial-response semantics relative to AppendFuture.Response contract.','Automatic snapshot creation/compaction, forced RecoverCluster and store-specific crash behavior remain deferred.','No executed operation history, property evidence, or overall correctness conclusion exists.'])\nsurfaces=[dict(entry_point='VerifyLeader / verifyLeader / verifyFuture.vote',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b-verify','b-heartbeat','b-notify-replication'],reason='Threshold counts voters but registrations cover all replication workers. Compare actual nonvoter contribution with API authority promise; lease and negative responses are 